  "worked_solution": "We find the ranges of the individual pieces, and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [-3,1]$ is $[-2,1]$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (1,3)$ is $(-3,1)$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $[-2,1]\\cup (-3,1)=(-3,1].$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the value $y=-3$ is NOT a valid output of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use parentheses $(…)$ instead of brackets $[…]$ at this endpoint.",
